    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (74.86) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) anchor the Austin Waves lineup as our elite plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong matchup against Freddy Peralta; while the park factor is slightly negative, the combination of Peralta\u2019s slower delivery\u2014which boosts **Gunnar Henderson**'s stolen base probability\u2014and a significant platoon advantage makes him our highest-ceiling asset. **Jacob Wilson**, assuming he holds his leadoff/two-hole position, is bolstered by a +19% SP skill advantage against Cody Bradford. **Jackson Merrill** (69.71) also warrants attention as a high-floor start against Tanner Bibee, with his dynamic platoon advantage (R/R) and favorable position in the five-hole providing a reliable base for runs and RBI production.\n\nStrategic caution is required elsewhere, particularly against tough arms like Dylan Cease. We are starting **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (55.84) and **Heliot Ramos** (44.01) despite Cease's 2.95 xERA, as their platoon profiles offer the best opportunity to mitigate the strikeout risk inherent in that matchup. The most difficult decision today was leaving **Coby Mayo** (42.34) on the bench. **Coby Mayo** was the last man out; while he offers power potential, his projected drop-off due to an assumed #8 batting order position made him less efficient than the consolidated production we expect from **Jackson Merrill** or **Dominic Smith** in higher-leverage spots. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the lineup status for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**, who are both currently \"Lineup Pending\" against Logan Henderson. While their base scores remain respectable, their utility is heavily tied to their placement in the order; if either is pushed to the bottom of the lineup, their efficiency scores will dip toward the marginal threshold. Furthermore, **Luis Robert Jr.** faces a notable downgrade today due to a -15% dynamic platoon hit against the opposing arm, though his sprint speed remains a vital asset for our stolen base targets. Ensure you monitor the confirmed cards, as any unexpected benching for **Andy Pages** or **Kyle Tucker** would necessitate a rotation shift to prioritize high-OBP alternatives like **Wade Meckler** from the bench.",
